# Appwrite SDK for Godot

This sdk provide support for Auth, Databases, Storage, Functions, Teams, and more.

[SDK Usage Example](https://nikhil0verma.github.io/Godot-Appwrite-client-SDK/)

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This project is community-maintained and is not officially maintained by Appwrite.

## Installation

### Godot 4.7+

1. Open the AssetStore tab inside the Godot 4.7+ editor.
2. Search for {{ spec.info.title }} SDK.
3. Download and install plugin.
4. Enable the plugin from Project -> Project Settings -> Plugins.

### Godot 4

1. Open Asset Store on web and search [{{ spec.info.title }} SDK](https://store.godotengine.org/asset/runn/appwrite-sdk).
2. Download and extract the zip file.
3. Copy the addon and .env.example to root of the project.
4. Enable the plugin from Project -> Project Settings -> Plugins.

## Getting Started

The plugin automatically intializes itself using values from .env. You can also set them at runtime using the `set_endpoint()`, `set_project()` and `set_self_signed()` methods.

### Quick Test connection to Appwrite server 

```gdscript
extends Node

func _ready():
    {{spec.info.title | caseUcfirst}}.ping()
